<UserControl xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
             xmlns:d="http://schemas.microsoft.com/expression/blend/2008"
             xmlns:mc="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/markup-compatibility/2006"
             xmlns:vm="using:DemoViewer.NET.ViewModels.MatchOverview"
             mc:Ignorable="d" d:DesignWidth="1180" d:DesignHeight="760"
             x:Class="DemoViewer.NET.Views.MatchOverview.MatchOverviewTabView"
             x:DataType="vm:MatchOverviewTabViewModel">

    <!--
        Match Overview — THE PER-DEMO PAGE. It does two jobs with one layout:
          • LIVE   — a demo is opening; the shell pushes pipeline state in and the slots fill.
          • CACHED — any indexed demo is rendered from its DemoCacheRecord. Nothing runs, nothing arrives.
        Because both modes paint the same sections from the same slots, opening a demo you were previewing
        has NO visual discontinuity: the cached render IS the skeleton the live fill lands into.

        SKELETON-FIRST (still the load-bearing rule): every section is in the tree from the FIRST rendered
        frame and only ever swaps its VALUES. Nothing is IsVisible-toggled on LOAD STATE, and the roster /
        scoreboard / highlight cards carry MinHeight so arriving rows fill reserved space instead of growing
        the page. If you add a section, give it a reserved slot and a placeholder.

        The one axis that IS allowed to toggle visibility is the FEATURE GATE (user-initiated, reconciled
        live, stable for a whole load) — a different thing entirely from load state. Nothing on this page
        does that yet; the highlight section will when it binds tab.highlights.

        PARTIAL FILL is the normal state, and the completeness chip is the honest answer to it: the page
        names the tier it has (LIVE / FULL / INDEXED / NOT INDEXED / FAILED) and every empty slot carries ONE
        sentence plus the single action that fills it — never a wall of "—", which in a cached render would
        read as "still loading" about a page where nothing is running.

        DESIGN NOTES (docs/ui/design-system.md, docs/ui/highlights-matchoverview-redesign.md):
          • Merged HERO BAND: identity + score plate + completeness chip + progress rail in ONE
            fixed-height slot, so both headline facts are above the fold and the band never changes height.
          • Two-column BODY at >= 1000px: "the match" (rosters + scoreboard) at 1.3*, "the moments"
            (highlights + enrichments) at *. Below the breakpoint they stack — one Grid, bound Column/Row/
            ColumnSpan, no duplicated subtree.
          • Team identity rides coloured LEFT strips + dots, NEVER header text: CT AccentInteractive fails AA
            as text on CardBg, so colour is the redundant cue and the word is the carrier (the StatusChip
            rule). CT = AccentInteractive, T = AccentAmber — the app-wide scoreboard convention.
          • Every colour is a {DynamicResource} palette token, so the page re-themes live.
    -->

    <Design.DataContext>
        <vm:MatchOverviewTabViewModel />
    </Design.DataContext>

    <UserControl.Styles>

        <!-- Hero brand bar — a short accent rule under the map name. -->
        <Style Selector="Rectangle.heroAccent">
            <Setter Property="Fill" Value="{DynamicResource AccentInteractive}" />
            <Setter Property="Height" Value="3" />
            <Setter Property="Width" Value="52" />
            <Setter Property="RadiusX" Value="1.5" />
            <Setter Property="RadiusY" Value="1.5" />
            <Setter Property="HorizontalAlignment" Value="Left" />
        </Style>

        <!-- Eyebrow — the small uppercase page label above the map name. TextMid (not the dimmer TextDim)
             so it clears ~AA on the shell background in dark/light; comfortably passes in High Contrast. -->
        <Style Selector="TextBlock.eyebrow">
            <Setter Property="FontFamily" Value="Consolas,Menlo,monospace" />
            <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="11" />
            <Setter Property="FontWeight" Value="SemiBold" />
            <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource TextMid}" />
        </Style>

        <!-- Section label — names a card without competing with its content. -->
        <Style Selector="TextBlock.sectionLabel">
            <Setter Property="FontFamily" Value="Consolas,Menlo,monospace" />
            <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="10" />
            <Setter Property="FontWeight" Value="SemiBold" />
            <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource TextMid}" />
            <Setter Property="Margin" Value="2 0 0 6" />
        </Style>

        <!-- Quick-fact tile — tiny label over a prominent value. Informational (labels the number below),
             so TextMid rather than the whisper-dim TextDim: ~4.3:1 dark / 7.4:1 light / 15.6:1 HC. -->
        <Style Selector="TextBlock.factLabel">
            <Setter Property="FontFamily" Value="Consolas,Menlo,monospace" />
            <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="10" />
            <Setter Property="FontWeight" Value="SemiBold" />
            <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource TextMid}" />
        </Style>
        <Style Selector="TextBlock.factValue">
            <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="21" />
            <Setter Property="FontWeight" Value="SemiBold" />
            <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource TextCardHeader}" />
        </Style>

        <!-- Stage strip — one step per open phase. Pending is dim; active brightens; done stays readable so
             the strip reads as a completed trail rather than emptying out. In a CACHED render every step is
             pending: nothing ran, and marking them done would claim a pipeline that never executed. -->
        <Style Selector="TextBlock.stageLabel">
            <Setter Property="FontFamily" Value="Consolas,Menlo,monospace" />
            <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="10.5" />
            <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource TextDim}" />
            <Setter Property="VerticalAlignment" Value="Center" />
        </Style>
        <Style Selector="TextBlock.stageLabel.done">
            <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource TextMid}" />
        </Style>
        <Style Selector="TextBlock.stageLabel.active">
            <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource TextCardHeader}" />
            <Setter Property="FontWeight" Value="SemiBold" />
        </Style>

        <!-- Completeness chip label — the state, in WORDS. Never tinted by state: the dot is the redundant
             colour cue and TextMid is the only token that clears AA on every theme (the StatusChip rule). -->
        <Style Selector="TextBlock.completenessLabel">
            <Setter Property="FontFamily" Value="Consolas,Menlo,monospace" />
            <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="11.5" />
            <Setter Property="FontWeight" Value="SemiBold" />
            <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource TextMid}" />
            <Setter Property="VerticalAlignment" Value="Center" />
            <Setter Property="TextTrimming" Value="CharacterEllipsis" />
        </Style>

        <!-- Score plate — the two big team numbers. -->
        <Style Selector="TextBlock.scoreValue">
            <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="38" />
            <Setter Property="FontWeight" Value="Bold" />
            <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource TextCardHeader}" />
            <Setter Property="VerticalAlignment" Value="Center" />
        </Style>
        <Style Selector="TextBlock.scoreSide">
            <Setter Property="FontFamily" Value="Consolas,Menlo,monospace" />
            <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="11" />
            <Setter Property="FontWeight" Value="SemiBold" />
            <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource TextMid}" />
        </Style>

        <!-- Roster header band — neutral text, team colour on the left strip. Mirrors Stats' teamHeader. -->
        <Style Selector="Border.rosterHeader">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource PanelHeaderBg}" />
            <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="{DynamicResource AccentAmber}" />
            <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="3 0 0 0" />
            <Setter Property="Padding" Value="12 9" />
        </Style>
        <Style Selector="Border.rosterHeader.ct">
            <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="{DynamicResource AccentInteractive}" />
        </Style>

        <!-- Team dot — the redundant colour cue beside the neutral team name. -->
        <Style Selector="Ellipse.teamDot">
            <Setter Property="Width" Value="9" />
            <Setter Property="Height" Value="9" />
            <Setter Property="VerticalAlignment" Value="Center" />
            <Setter Property="Fill" Value="{DynamicResource AccentAmber}" />
        </Style>
        <Style Selector="Ellipse.teamDot.ct">
            <Setter Property="Fill" Value="{DynamicResource AccentInteractive}" />
        </Style>

        <Style Selector="TextBlock.rosterName">
            <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="13" />
            <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource TextValue}" />
            <Setter Property="VerticalAlignment" Value="Center" />
            <Setter Property="TextTrimming" Value="CharacterEllipsis" />
        </Style>

        <!-- BOT tag — an outlined chip; TextMid clears AA on the card surface in every theme. -->
        <Style Selector="Border.botTag">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent" />
            <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="{DynamicResource BorderStrong}" />
            <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="1" />
            <Setter Property="CornerRadius" Value="3" />
            <Setter Property="Padding" Value="4 0" />
            <Setter Property="VerticalAlignment" Value="Center" />
            <Setter Property="Margin" Value="6 0 0 0" />
        </Style>
        <Style Selector="TextBlock.botTagText">
            <Setter Property="FontFamily" Value="Consolas,Menlo,monospace" />
            <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="9" />
            <Setter Property="FontWeight" Value="SemiBold" />
            <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource TextMid}" />
        </Style>

        <!-- Scoreboard — a compact fixed-column table (the Stats tab owns the sortable, full one). -->
        <Style Selector="TextBlock.sbHead">
            <Setter Property="FontFamily" Value="Consolas,Menlo,monospace" />
            <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="10" />
            <Setter Property="FontWeight" Value="SemiBold" />
            <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource TextMid}" />
            <Setter Property="TextAlignment" Value="Right" />
        </Style>
        <Style Selector="TextBlock.sbCell">
            <Setter Property="FontFamily" Value="Consolas,Menlo,monospace" />
            <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="12" />
            <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource TextValue}" />
            <Setter Property="TextAlignment" Value="Right" />
            <Setter Property="VerticalAlignment" Value="Center" />
        </Style>
        <Style Selector="Rectangle.sideBar">
            <Setter Property="Width" Value="3" />
            <Setter Property="Height" Value="14" />
            <Setter Property="RadiusX" Value="1.5" />
            <Setter Property="RadiusY" Value="1.5" />
            <Setter Property="Fill" Value="{DynamicResource AccentAmber}" />
            <Setter Property="VerticalAlignment" Value="Center" />
        </Style>
        <Style Selector="Rectangle.sideBar.ct">
            <Setter Property="Fill" Value="{DynamicResource AccentInteractive}" />
        </Style>

        <!-- Empty-slot message: one sentence naming the missing tier, beside the action that fills it.
             TextBRIGHT, not the whisper-dim TextDim it started as: in an empty card this sentence IS the
             primary content, and TextDim on CardBg measures 1.81:1 in Dark — far under AA, and the same
             defect that already moved this page's fact micro-labels off TextDim. TextBright is 7.17:1 dark /
             9.89:1 light, so the one thing the user must read to understand the empty card is readable. -->
        <Style Selector="TextBlock.slotMessage">
            <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="12.5" />
            <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource TextBright}" />
            <Setter Property="TextWrapping" Value="Wrap" />
        </Style>

        <!-- Highlight row metadata (round / tick). Secondary to the title, but still text a user reads, so
             TextMid (4.26:1 dark / 7.37:1 light) rather than TextFrameInfo's 3.48:1 dark. The title above
             stays TextBright, so the hierarchy is intact without pushing the metadata under the floor. -->
        <Style Selector="TextBlock.hlMeta">
            <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="11" />
            <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource TextMid}" />
            <Setter Property="VerticalAlignment" Value="Center" />
        </Style>

        <!-- Not-known-yet value. The placeholder keeps the slot at full size (no reflow) but drops to the
             dim token so an unfilled "—" reads as waiting rather than as a redacted block — which is exactly
             how a bold 40px em-dash reads at full contrast. Value-driven, never layout-driven.
             MUST stay LAST in this block: Avalonia resolves competing setters by declaration order, not
             selector specificity, so an earlier .pending would silently lose to .factValue/.scoreValue. -->
        <Style Selector="TextBlock.pending">
            <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource TextDim}" />
            <Setter Property="FontWeight" Value="Normal" />
        </Style>

    </UserControl.Styles>

    <Panel>

        <!-- ── Empty state — no demo open or previewed. ─────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
        <StackPanel IsVisible="{Binding !HasContent}"
                    HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Center" Spacing="10" MaxWidth="380">
            <Rectangle Classes="heroAccent" HorizontalAlignment="Center" />
            <TextBlock Text="No demo selected"
                       Foreground="{DynamicResource TextCardHeader}"
                       FontSize="19" FontWeight="SemiBold" HorizontalAlignment="Center" />
            <TextBlock
                Text="Pick a demo in your Library to see its overview here — instantly, from the index. Open it to go deeper."
                Foreground="{DynamicResource TextDim}" TextAlignment="Center"
                FontSize="13" TextWrapping="Wrap" HorizontalAlignment="Center" />
        </StackPanel>

        <!-- ── Content — the full skeleton, present from the first frame in EVERY mode. ─────────────── -->
        <ScrollViewer IsVisible="{Binding HasContent}" Padding="28 24"
                      HorizontalScrollBarVisibility="Disabled">
            <StackPanel Spacing="14" MaxWidth="1180" HorizontalAlignment="Stretch">

                <!--
                    ══ HERO BAND ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
                    Identity + score + completeness + progress in ONE fixed-height slot. The two
                    things a user opens a demo to see are the map and the score, so they share the top row;
                    the state line and the progress rail sit under a divider inside the same card. MinHeight
                    is what keeps the band identical across modes and load states.
                -->
                <Border Classes="card" Padding="22 18" MinHeight="168">
                    <Grid RowDefinitions="Auto,Auto,Auto" RowSpacing="12">

                        <!-- Identity (left) | score plate (right). -->
                        <Grid Grid.Row="0" ColumnDefinitions="*,Auto" ColumnSpacing="20">

                            <!-- MinHeight reserves the identity block so a demo whose map name has not been
                                 read yet (the cheap header read can miss) does not shrink the band and then
                                 grow it when the name arrives. -->
                            <StackPanel Grid.Column="0" Spacing="5" MinHeight="92" VerticalAlignment="Top">
                                <TextBlock Text="MATCH OVERVIEW" Classes="eyebrow" />
                                <TextBlock Text="{Binding MapDisplay}"
                                           IsVisible="{Binding MapDisplay, Converter={x:Static StringConverters.IsNotNullOrEmpty}}"
                                           Foreground="{DynamicResource TextCardHeader}"
                                           FontSize="30" FontWeight="Bold" TextWrapping="Wrap" LineHeight="34" />
                                <Rectangle Classes="heroAccent" Margin="0 1 0 3" />
                                <TextBlock Text="{Binding ServerName}"
                                           IsVisible="{Binding ServerName, Converter={x:Static StringConverters.IsNotNullOrEmpty}}"
                                           Foreground="{DynamicResource TextMid}"
                                           FontSize="12.5" TextWrapping="Wrap" />
                                <TextBlock Text="{Binding FileName}"
                                           Foreground="{DynamicResource TextDim}"
                                           Classes="mono" FontSize="11.5" TextWrapping="Wrap" />
                            </StackPanel>

                            <!--
                                Score plate. WORDING IS LOAD-BEARING: each number is a TEAM's total for the
                                whole match, and a team is identified by its clan name or by the side it
                                FINISHED on ("ENDED CT"), because sides swap at the half. They are NOT the
                                rounds won by that side — the earlier wording said exactly that and was false
                                (on the reference demo the team ending CT totalled 3 while the CT side won 15
                                of 16). The honest per-side split is its own row in the left column below.
                                Do not shorten these labels back to bare side names.
                            -->
                            <StackPanel Grid.Column="1" Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="14"
                                        VerticalAlignment="Center" MinWidth="270"
                                        HorizontalAlignment="Right">
                                <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="10" VerticalAlignment="Center">
                                    <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="6" VerticalAlignment="Center">
                                        <Ellipse Classes="teamDot ct" />
                                        <TextBlock Text="{Binding CtTeamLabel}" Classes="scoreSide"
                                                   VerticalAlignment="Center" MaxWidth="112"
                                                   TextTrimming="CharacterEllipsis" />
                                    </StackPanel>
                                    <TextBlock Text="{Binding CtTeamScoreDisplay}" Classes="scoreValue"
                                               Classes.pending="{Binding !HasScore}" />
                                </StackPanel>
                                <TextBlock Text="–" Foreground="{DynamicResource TextDim}"
                                           FontSize="24" VerticalAlignment="Center" />
                                <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="10" VerticalAlignment="Center">
                                    <TextBlock Text="{Binding TTeamScoreDisplay}" Classes="scoreValue"
                                               Classes.pending="{Binding !HasScore}" />
                                    <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="6" VerticalAlignment="Center">
                                        <Ellipse Classes="teamDot" />
                                        <TextBlock Text="{Binding TTeamLabel}" Classes="scoreSide"
                                                   VerticalAlignment="Center" MaxWidth="112"
                                                   TextTrimming="CharacterEllipsis" />
                                    </StackPanel>
                                </StackPanel>
                            </StackPanel>
                        </Grid>

                        <Rectangle Grid.Row="1" Classes="divider" Height="1" HorizontalAlignment="Stretch" />

                        <!-- Completeness row + progress rail. -->
                        <Grid Grid.Row="2" RowDefinitions="Auto,Auto" RowSpacing="9">

                            <!--
                                THE COMPLETENESS CHIP. Dot + word + the single action that advances the state.
                                The dot reuses the shared Ellipse.dot.* classes (bound class → palette token,
                                never a brush on the view-model), so it re-themes for free; INDEXED is the
                                HOLLOW good ring — the established "partial, not the whole story" treatment.
                                The label is NEVER tinted by state: WCAG 1.4.1, and TextMid is the only token
                                that clears AA on this surface in all four built-in themes.
                            -->
                            <!-- MinHeight RESERVES the action row. The buttons only exist in the cached and
                                 failed states, so without it the band grew ~16px the moment a preview was
                                 rendered — a mode switch that moved the page, which is the same defect as a
                                 load that moves it. Measured by MatchOverviewLandingTests. -->
                            <Grid Grid.Row="0" ColumnDefinitions="Auto,*,Auto" ColumnSpacing="10"
                                  MinHeight="32">
                                <StackPanel Grid.Column="0" Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="8"
                                            VerticalAlignment="Center">
                                    <!-- ONE element carries every state class. `.stateGood` + `.hollow`
                                         together ARE the partial ring: the solid selectors are declared
                                         `:not(.hollow)`, so the pair resolves to the Stroke rule and cannot
                                         collide. (This was briefly two overlapping ellipses pulled together
                                         by a negative margin that silently depended on the parent's
                                         Spacing — the selectors already make that unnecessary.) -->
                                    <Ellipse Width="10" Height="10"
                                             Classes="dot"
                                             Classes.stateWorking="{Binding IsCompletenessWorking}"
                                             Classes.pulsing="{Binding IsCompletenessWorking}"
                                             Classes.stateGood="{Binding IsCompletenessGood}"
                                             Classes.hollow="{Binding IsCompletenessPartial}"
                                             Classes.stateError="{Binding IsCompletenessError}"
                                             Classes.stateOff="{Binding IsCompletenessOff}" />
                                    <TextBlock Text="{Binding CompletenessLabel}" Classes="completenessLabel"
                                               MaxWidth="360" />
                                </StackPanel>

                                <!-- Actions. A WrapPanel so a narrow band reflows rather than clipping the
                                     primary CTA — the responsive-strip rule. -->
                                <WrapPanel Grid.Column="2" Orientation="Horizontal" HorizontalAlignment="Right"
                                           VerticalAlignment="Center">
                                    <Button Classes="chip" Content="◀ Back"
                                            IsVisible="{Binding CanReturnToLive}"
                                            Command="{Binding ReturnToLiveCommand}"
                                            FontSize="11" Padding="10 4" Margin="0 2 8 2"
                                            ToolTip.Tip="{Binding LiveDemoName, StringFormat='Back to {0}'}" />
                                    <Button Classes="chip" Content="{Binding CompletenessActionLabel}"
                                            IsVisible="{Binding HasCompletenessAction}"
                                            Command="{Binding ComputeFullStatsCommand}"
                                            FontSize="11" Padding="12 4" Margin="0 2 8 2"
                                            ToolTip.Tip="Queue this demo for a full analysis pass — it runs in the background and never opens the demo" />
                                    <Button Classes="primary" Content="Open this demo"
                                            IsVisible="{Binding IsCached}"
                                            IsEnabled="{Binding CanOpenDemo}"
                                            Command="{Binding OpenDemoCommand}"
                                            FontSize="12" Padding="14 5" Margin="0 2 0 2" />
                                </WrapPanel>
                            </Grid>

                            <!--
                                Progress rail. A thin bar + the three stage words on one line — one sixth the
                                height of the old stage card, and the completeness chip above now carries the
                                state word the card used to. The eased transition is half of what makes it
                                feel smooth: the VM creeps the value in ~90 ms steps toward the active stage's
                                ceiling, and a 300 ms ease turns those steps into continuous motion AND
                                softens the real stage-boundary jumps, which are large.
                            -->
                            <Grid Grid.Row="1" ColumnDefinitions="*,Auto" ColumnSpacing="16">
                                <ProgressBar Grid.Column="0" Minimum="0" Maximum="1" Value="{Binding Progress}"
                                             Height="3" CornerRadius="1.5" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                             Foreground="{DynamicResource AccentInteractive}"
                                             Background="{DynamicResource PanelHeaderBg}">
                                    <ProgressBar.Transitions>
                                        <Transitions>
                                            <DoubleTransition Property="Value" Duration="0:0:0.3"
                                                              Easing="CubicEaseOut" />
                                        </Transitions>
                                    </ProgressBar.Transitions>
                                </ProgressBar>

                                <!-- Fixed-length list built once in the ctor — rows are never added or
                                     removed, only their flags flip. -->
                                <ItemsControl Grid.Column="1" ItemsSource="{Binding Stages}">
                                    <ItemsControl.ItemsPanel>
                                        <ItemsPanelTemplate>
                                            <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="14" />
                                        </ItemsPanelTemplate>
                                    </ItemsControl.ItemsPanel>
                                    <ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
                                        <DataTemplate x:DataType="vm:LoadStageViewModel">
                                            <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="6">
                                                <Ellipse Width="6" Height="6" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                                         Fill="{DynamicResource BorderStrong}"
                                                         IsVisible="{Binding !IsDone}" />
                                                <Ellipse Width="6" Height="6" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                                         Fill="{DynamicResource AccentInteractive}"
                                                         IsVisible="{Binding IsDone}" />
                                                <TextBlock Text="{Binding Label}" Classes="stageLabel"
                                                           Classes.active="{Binding IsActive}"
                                                           Classes.done="{Binding IsDone}" />
                                            </StackPanel>
                                        </DataTemplate>
                                    </ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
                                </ItemsControl>
                            </Grid>
                        </Grid>
                    </Grid>
                </Border>

                <!-- Bundled-sample banner: the tour demo is a deliberate few-round trim, so its score is
                     partial BY DESIGN — say so up front or the truncated score reads as a scoring bug. Only
                     ever true for the shipped assets/tour sample. Additive, never a replacement. -->
                <Border IsVisible="{Binding IsSampleClip}"
                        Background="{DynamicResource ChainSummaryBadgeBg}"
                        BorderBrush="{DynamicResource BorderSubtle}" BorderThickness="1"
                        CornerRadius="4" Padding="10 6" HorizontalAlignment="Left">
                    <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="8">
                        <TextBlock Text="SAMPLE CLIP" FontSize="11" FontWeight="Bold"
                                   Foreground="{DynamicResource AccentAmber}" VerticalAlignment="Center" />
                        <TextBlock
                            Text="the first few rounds of a real match, bundled to explore with — scores show a partial result"
                            Foreground="{DynamicResource TextMid}" FontSize="12"
                            TextWrapping="Wrap" VerticalAlignment="Center" />
                    </StackPanel>
                </Border>

                <!-- Damaged-demo banner (S11 diagnostics channel, v0.6.0): the parse recovered but
                     reported structured warnings — rejected string tables, dropped player blobs — so a
                     page full of "—" placeholders now explains itself instead of reading as a scoring
                     bug. Same additive-banner grammar as the sample-clip banner above. -->
                <Border IsVisible="{Binding IsDamaged}"
                        Background="{DynamicResource ChainSummaryBadgeBg}"
                        BorderBrush="{DynamicResource BorderSubtle}" BorderThickness="1"
                        CornerRadius="4" Padding="10 6" HorizontalAlignment="Left">
                    <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="8">
                        <TextBlock Text="⚠ THIS DEMO MAY BE DAMAGED" FontSize="11" FontWeight="Bold"
                                   Foreground="{DynamicResource AccentAmber}" VerticalAlignment="Center" />
                        <TextBlock Text="{Binding DamageSummary}"
                                   Foreground="{DynamicResource TextMid}" FontSize="12"
                                   TextWrapping="Wrap" VerticalAlignment="Center" />
                    </StackPanel>
                </Border>

                <!-- Failure detail — the ONE conditional block on the page. It is additive (an error line
                     appended below a stable layout), never a replacement for a section. -->
                <Border Classes="card" Padding="20 14" IsVisible="{Binding Failed}">
                    <TextBlock Text="{Binding ErrorText}"
                               Foreground="{DynamicResource TextMid}"
                               FontSize="12.5" TextWrapping="Wrap" />
                </Border>

                <!-- ══ FACTS STRIP ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
                     Values swap placeholder → real; the card never changes size. SPECTATORS sits in Auto
                     columns rather than a star column, and it and its divider gate on HasSpectators: most
                     demos have none, and an Auto column whose only child is collapsed takes zero width, so
                     the row stays a clean four-tile layout instead of carrying a permanently-empty cell. -->
                <Border Classes="card" Padding="20 14">
                    <Grid ColumnDefinitions="*,Auto,*,Auto,*,Auto,Auto,Auto,*">
                        <StackPanel Grid.Column="0" Spacing="3">
                            <TextBlock Text="DURATION" Classes="factLabel" />
                            <TextBlock Text="{Binding DurationDisplay}" Classes="factValue"
                                       Classes.pending="{Binding !HasSummary}" />
                        </StackPanel>
                        <Rectangle Grid.Column="1" Classes="divider" Width="1" Margin="18 2"
                                   VerticalAlignment="Stretch" />
                        <StackPanel Grid.Column="2" Spacing="3">
                            <TextBlock Text="ROUNDS" Classes="factLabel" />
                            <TextBlock Text="{Binding RoundCountDisplay}" Classes="factValue"
                                       Classes.pending="{Binding !HasSummary}" />
                        </StackPanel>
                        <Rectangle Grid.Column="3" Classes="divider" Width="1" Margin="18 2"
                                   VerticalAlignment="Stretch" />
                        <StackPanel Grid.Column="4" Spacing="3">
                            <TextBlock Text="PLAYERS" Classes="factLabel" />
                            <TextBlock Text="{Binding PlayerCountDisplay}" Classes="factValue"
                                       Classes.pending="{Binding !HasSummary}" />
                        </StackPanel>
                        <Rectangle Grid.Column="5" Classes="divider" Width="1" Margin="18 2"
                                   VerticalAlignment="Stretch"
                                   IsVisible="{Binding HasSpectators}" />
                        <StackPanel Grid.Column="6" Spacing="3"
                                    IsVisible="{Binding HasSpectators}"
                                    ToolTip.Tip="Named accounts in the demo with no team — observers, coaches, admins. Excluded from PLAYERS so that number matches the rosters below.">
                            <TextBlock Text="SPECTATORS" Classes="factLabel" />
                            <TextBlock Text="{Binding SpectatorCountDisplay}" Classes="factValue"
                                       Classes.pending="{Binding !HasSummary}" />
                        </StackPanel>
                        <Rectangle Grid.Column="7" Classes="divider" Width="1" Margin="18 2"
                                   VerticalAlignment="Stretch" />
                        <StackPanel Grid.Column="8" Spacing="3">
                            <TextBlock Text="TICK RATE" Classes="factLabel" />
                            <TextBlock Text="{Binding TickRateDisplay}" Classes="factValue"
                                       Classes.pending="{Binding !HasSummary}" />
                        </StackPanel>
                    </Grid>
                </Border>

                <!--
                    ══ BODY — two columns at >= 1000px, stacked below ════════════════════════
                    ONE Grid, never two stacked layouts: the two groups bind Grid.Column / Grid.Row /
                    Grid.ColumnSpan to view-model ints, so exactly one arrangement is realised and there is no
                    duplicated subtree to drift. The column ratio is 1.3* : * — "the match" is the denser
                    column (two rosters + a ten-row scoreboard).
                -->
                <Grid ColumnDefinitions="1.3*,20,*" RowDefinitions="Auto,Auto" RowSpacing="14">

                    <!-- ── THE MATCH — rosters, scoreboard, side split, explore CTAs ──────────────── -->
                    <StackPanel Grid.Row="0" Grid.Column="0"
                                Grid.ColumnSpan="{Binding MatchColumnSpan}" Spacing="14">

                        <!-- Rosters — CT / T side by side. MinHeight reserves a 5-a-side roster so arriving
                             names FILL the card instead of growing it (the jump this page exists to remove).
                             A side with more than five players still grows; that is the honest limit of a
                             fixed slot. Measured against real rendered layout by MatchOverviewLandingTests. -->
                        <Grid ColumnDefinitions="*,14,*">
                            <Border Grid.Column="0" Classes="card" ClipToBounds="True" MinHeight="188">
                                <DockPanel>
                                    <Border DockPanel.Dock="Top" Classes="rosterHeader ct">
                                        <Grid ColumnDefinitions="Auto,8,*,Auto">
                                            <Ellipse Grid.Column="0" Classes="teamDot ct" />
                                            <TextBlock Grid.Column="2" Text="Counter-Terrorists"
                                                       Foreground="{DynamicResource TextCardHeader}"
                                                       FontSize="13" FontWeight="SemiBold"
                                                       VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                                       TextTrimming="CharacterEllipsis" />
                                            <Border Grid.Column="3" Classes="badge" VerticalAlignment="Center">
                                                <TextBlock Text="{Binding CtRosterCountDisplay}"
                                                           Classes="mono" FontSize="11"
                                                           Foreground="{DynamicResource TextChainBadge}" />
                                            </Border>
                                        </Grid>
                                    </Border>
                                    <!-- The missing-tier message shares the reserved slot with the rows, so
                                         a roster that cannot be split says why instead of drawing an empty
                                         team. Same treatment as the scoreboard's third state. -->
                                    <TextBlock DockPanel.Dock="Top" Text="{Binding RosterMessage}"
                                               IsVisible="{Binding RosterMessage, Converter={x:Static StringConverters.IsNotNullOrEmpty}}"
                                               Classes="slotMessage" Margin="14 12" />
                                    <ItemsControl ItemsSource="{Binding CounterTerrorists}" Margin="14 10 14 12">
                                        <ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
                                            <DataTemplate x:DataType="vm:OverviewPlayer">
                                                <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Margin="0 3">
                                                    <TextBlock Text="{Binding Name}" Classes="rosterName" />
                                                    <Border Classes="botTag" IsVisible="{Binding IsBot}">
                                                        <TextBlock Text="BOT" Classes="botTagText" />
                                                    </Border>
                                                </StackPanel>
                                            </DataTemplate>
                                        </ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
                                    </ItemsControl>
                                </DockPanel>
                            </Border>

                            <Border Grid.Column="2" Classes="card" ClipToBounds="True" MinHeight="188">
                                <DockPanel>
                                    <Border DockPanel.Dock="Top" Classes="rosterHeader">
                                        <Grid ColumnDefinitions="Auto,8,*,Auto">
                                            <Ellipse Grid.Column="0" Classes="teamDot" />
                                            <TextBlock Grid.Column="2" Text="Terrorists"
                                                       Foreground="{DynamicResource TextCardHeader}"
                                                       FontSize="13" FontWeight="SemiBold"
                                                       VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                                       TextTrimming="CharacterEllipsis" />
                                            <Border Grid.Column="3" Classes="badge" VerticalAlignment="Center">
                                                <TextBlock Text="{Binding TRosterCountDisplay}"
                                                           Classes="mono" FontSize="11"
                                                           Foreground="{DynamicResource TextChainBadge}" />
                                            </Border>
                                        </Grid>
                                    </Border>
                                    <TextBlock DockPanel.Dock="Top" Text="{Binding RosterMessage}"
                                               IsVisible="{Binding RosterMessage, Converter={x:Static StringConverters.IsNotNullOrEmpty}}"
                                               Classes="slotMessage" Margin="14 12" />
                                    <ItemsControl ItemsSource="{Binding Terrorists}" Margin="14 10 14 12">
                                        <ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
                                            <DataTemplate x:DataType="vm:OverviewPlayer">
                                                <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Margin="0 3">
                                                    <TextBlock Text="{Binding Name}" Classes="rosterName" />
                                                    <Border Classes="botTag" IsVisible="{Binding IsBot}">
                                                        <TextBlock Text="BOT" Classes="botTagText" />
                                                    </Border>
                                                </StackPanel>
                                            </DataTemplate>
                                        </ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
                                    </ItemsControl>
                                </DockPanel>
                            </Border>
                        </Grid>

                        <!-- Scoreboard. Reserved height for a FULL 10-player lobby; the "needs a full
                             analysis pass" / "ran but produced nothing" message occupies the same slot, so a
                             skeleton never hangs forever and a cached page says what would fill it. -->
                        <StackPanel Spacing="0">
                            <TextBlock Text="PLAYER STATS" Classes="sectionLabel" />
                            <Border Classes="card" ClipToBounds="True" MinHeight="268">
                                <DockPanel>
                                    <Border DockPanel.Dock="Top" Background="{DynamicResource PanelHeaderBg}"
                                            Padding="14 8">
                                        <Grid ColumnDefinitions="3,9,*,50,50,50,60,60">
                                            <TextBlock Grid.Column="2" Text="PLAYER" Classes="sbHead"
                                                       TextAlignment="Left" />
                                            <TextBlock Grid.Column="3" Text="K" Classes="sbHead" />
                                            <TextBlock Grid.Column="4" Text="D" Classes="sbHead" />
                                            <TextBlock Grid.Column="5" Text="A" Classes="sbHead" />
                                            <TextBlock Grid.Column="6" Text="ADR" Classes="sbHead" />
                                            <TextBlock Grid.Column="7" Text="RATING" Classes="sbHead" />
                                        </Grid>
                                    </Border>

                                    <!-- The missing-tier message + its action, inside the reserved slot. -->
                                    <StackPanel DockPanel.Dock="Top" Margin="14 12" Spacing="9"
                                                IsVisible="{Binding PlayerStatsMessage, Converter={x:Static StringConverters.IsNotNullOrEmpty}}">
                                        <TextBlock Text="{Binding PlayerStatsMessage}" Classes="slotMessage" />
                                        <Button Classes="chip" Content="{Binding CompletenessActionLabel}"
                                                IsVisible="{Binding HasCompletenessAction}"
                                                Command="{Binding ComputeFullStatsCommand}"
                                                FontSize="11" Padding="12 4" HorizontalAlignment="Left" />
                                    </StackPanel>

                                    <ItemsControl ItemsSource="{Binding PlayerStats}" Margin="14 8 14 10">
                                        <ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
                                            <DataTemplate x:DataType="vm:OverviewStatRow">
                                                <Grid ColumnDefinitions="3,9,*,50,50,50,60,60" Margin="0 3">
                                                    <Rectangle Grid.Column="0" Classes="sideBar"
                                                               Classes.ct="{Binding IsCt}" />
                                                    <TextBlock Grid.Column="2" Text="{Binding Name}"
                                                               Classes="rosterName" />
                                                    <TextBlock Grid.Column="3" Text="{Binding Kills}" Classes="sbCell" />
                                                    <TextBlock Grid.Column="4" Text="{Binding Deaths}" Classes="sbCell" />
                                                    <TextBlock Grid.Column="5" Text="{Binding Assists}"
                                                               Classes="sbCell" />
                                                    <TextBlock Grid.Column="6" Text="{Binding Adr}" Classes="sbCell" />
                                                    <TextBlock Grid.Column="7" Text="{Binding Rating}" Classes="sbCell"
                                                               Foreground="{DynamicResource TextCardHeader}" />
                                                </Grid>
                                            </DataTemplate>
                                        </ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
                                    </ItemsControl>
                                </DockPanel>
                            </Border>
                        </StackPanel>

                        <!-- The genuinely per-side split. Analysis-derived, so it shows ONLY when it
                             reconciles against the authoritative score (HasSideSplit) — on HLTV demos the
                             CTW/TW columns collapse and would otherwise print a 0/1 "split" of a 14-round
                             match. The row keeps its slot either way: the no-jump rule applies to a
                             suppressed value exactly as it does to a pending one. -->
                        <Panel Height="18">
                            <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="8" HorizontalAlignment="Center"
                                        VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                        IsVisible="{Binding HasSideSplit}">
                                <TextBlock Text="ROUNDS BY SIDE" Classes="factLabel" VerticalAlignment="Center" />
                                <Ellipse Classes="teamDot ct" Width="7" Height="7" />
                                <TextBlock Text="CT" Classes="scoreSide" VerticalAlignment="Center" />
                                <TextBlock Text="{Binding CtSideWinsDisplay}" Classes="mono"
                                           FontSize="13" FontWeight="SemiBold"
                                           Foreground="{DynamicResource TextCardHeader}"
                                           VerticalAlignment="Center" />
                                <TextBlock Text="·" Foreground="{DynamicResource TextDim}"
                                           Margin="4 0" VerticalAlignment="Center" />
                                <Ellipse Classes="teamDot" Width="7" Height="7" />
                                <TextBlock Text="T" Classes="scoreSide" VerticalAlignment="Center" />
                                <TextBlock Text="{Binding TSideWinsDisplay}" Classes="mono"
                                           FontSize="13" FontWeight="SemiBold"
                                           Foreground="{DynamicResource TextCardHeader}"
                                           VerticalAlignment="Center" />
                            </StackPanel>
                            <TextBlock Text="Per-side split unavailable for this demo"
                                       IsVisible="{Binding !HasSideSplit}"
                                       HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                       Foreground="{DynamicResource TextDim}" FontSize="11" />
                        </Panel>

                        <!-- Explore CTAs — always present; ENABLED (not shown) once the demo is explorable,
                             so the row never appears from nowhere. Both are mode-gated too: in a cached
                             render the Stats and 2D tabs hold a different demo, so the honest offer is
                             "Open this demo" in the hero band, not a jump to another match's scoreboard. -->
                        <WrapPanel Orientation="Horizontal">
                            <Button Classes="primary" Content="View full stats"
                                    Command="{Binding ViewStatsCommand}"
                                    IsEnabled="{Binding CanExploreStats}"
                                    Margin="0 0 10 0" Padding="16 7" />
                            <Button Classes="chip" Content="Watch in 2D"
                                    Command="{Binding ViewPlaybackCommand}"
                                    IsEnabled="{Binding CanExplorePlayback}"
                                    Padding="16 7" />
                        </WrapPanel>
                    </StackPanel>

                    <!-- ── THE MOMENTS — highlights + the enrichment slot ─────────────────────────── -->
                    <StackPanel Grid.Row="{Binding MomentsRow}" Grid.Column="{Binding MomentsColumn}"
                                Grid.ColumnSpan="{Binding MomentsColumnSpan}" Spacing="14">

                        <StackPanel Spacing="0">
                            <Grid ColumnDefinitions="Auto,*,Auto">
                                <TextBlock Grid.Column="0" Text="HIGHLIGHTS" Classes="sectionLabel" />
                                <TextBlock Grid.Column="2" Text="{Binding HighlightCountDisplay}"
                                           Classes="sectionLabel"
                                           IsVisible="{Binding HasHighlights}" />
                            </Grid>

                            <!--
                                Reserved so the section does not grow the page when moments arrive, and
                                BOUNDED above so it cannot run away.
                                  <= 300px of content -> the reserve (an empty or small set still holds its
                                     slot, same as the roster and scoreboard cards);
                                  300-620            -> grows, filling space beside the taller match column;
                                  > 620              -> the inner ScrollViewer takes over.
                                The upper bound matters more here than on the other cards: a roster is capped
                                at ~5 and a scoreboard at ~10, so their overflow is rare, but a demo can fire
                                thirty highlights and an unbounded card would dwarf the whole page. Growth
                                inside the band is CONTENT-driven (same demo -> same height), never
                                load-driven, so it cannot produce the mid-load jump the page forbids.
                            -->
                            <Border Classes="card" ClipToBounds="True" MinHeight="300" MaxHeight="620">
                                <DockPanel>
                                    <!-- Missing-tier message + its action, in the reserved slot. -->
                                    <StackPanel DockPanel.Dock="Top" Margin="14 14" Spacing="9"
                                                IsVisible="{Binding HighlightsMessage, Converter={x:Static StringConverters.IsNotNullOrEmpty}}">
                                        <TextBlock Text="{Binding HighlightsMessage}" Classes="slotMessage" />
                                        <!-- The highlight card owns its OWN action, not the chip's. They
                                             diverge in a common state: a finished live open has a real
                                             scoreboard (chip has nothing to advance) while highlights are
                                             still un-indexed, because they come from a different pass. -->
                                        <Button Classes="chip" Content="{Binding HighlightsActionLabel}"
                                                IsVisible="{Binding HasHighlightsAction}"
                                                Command="{Binding ComputeFullStatsCommand}"
                                                FontSize="11" Padding="12 4" HorizontalAlignment="Left" />
                                    </StackPanel>

                                    <ScrollViewer HorizontalScrollBarVisibility="Disabled">
                                        <ItemsControl ItemsSource="{Binding HighlightGroups}" Margin="8 8">
                                            <ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
                                                <DataTemplate x:DataType="vm:OverviewHighlightGroup">
                                                    <!-- Stretch both the Expander and its header content:
                                                         Fluent sizes an Expander to its content by default,
                                                         which left the per-player groups at ragged widths
                                                         inside the card. -->
                                                    <Expander IsExpanded="{Binding IsExpanded}" Padding="0"
                                                              Margin="0 0 0 4" Background="Transparent"
                                                              HorizontalAlignment="Stretch"
                                                              HorizontalContentAlignment="Stretch">
                                                        <Expander.Header>
                                                            <!-- Grid, not a StackPanel: the "Select all" button
                                                                 is pinned to the RIGHT of the header while the
                                                                 dot + name + count stay left. The button carries
                                                                 its OWN Click, so pressing it stages the section
                                                                 without also toggling the expander. -->
                                                            <Grid ColumnDefinitions="Auto,Auto,Auto,*,Auto"
                                                                  VerticalAlignment="Center">
                                                                <!-- Team colour is the dot, never the name:
                                                                     the page-wide contrast rule. -->
                                                                <Ellipse Grid.Column="0" Classes="teamDot"
                                                                         Classes.ct="{Binding IsCt}"
                                                                         Margin="0 0 8 0" />
                                                                <TextBlock Grid.Column="1" Text="{Binding PlayerName}"
                                                                           Foreground="{DynamicResource TextValue}"
                                                                           FontSize="13" FontWeight="SemiBold"
                                                                           VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                                                           TextTrimming="CharacterEllipsis" />
                                                                <TextBlock Grid.Column="2"
                                                                           Text="{Binding CountDisplay}"
                                                                           Classes="hlMeta" Margin="8 0 0 0" />
                                                                <Button Grid.Column="4" Classes="chip"
                                                                        Content="Select all"
                                                                        Command="{Binding SelectAllCommand}"
                                                                        FontSize="11" Padding="8 2" Margin="8 0"
                                                                        VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                                                        ToolTip.Tip="Stage every highlight in this player's section for a reel" />
                                                            </Grid>
                                                        </Expander.Header>
                                                        <ItemsControl ItemsSource="{Binding Highlights}"
                                                                      Margin="6 2 0 6">
                                                            <ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
                                                                <DataTemplate x:DataType="vm:OverviewHighlightRow">
                                                                    <Border
                                                                        BorderBrush="{DynamicResource HexRowSeparator}"
                                                                        BorderThickness="0 0 0 1" Padding="4 6">
                                                                        <Grid ColumnDefinitions="*,Auto,Auto,Auto,Auto"
                                                                              ColumnSpacing="8">
                                                                            <TextBlock Grid.Column="0"
                                                                                    Text="{Binding Title}"
                                                                                    Foreground="{DynamicResource TextBright}"
                                                                                    FontSize="12"
                                                                                    VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                                                                    TextTrimming="CharacterEllipsis" />
                                                                            <TextBlock Grid.Column="1"
                                                                                    Text="{Binding RoundDisplay}"
                                                                                    Classes="hlMeta" />
                                                                            <TextBlock Grid.Column="2"
                                                                                    Text="{Binding TickDisplay}"
                                                                                    Classes="hlMeta mono" />
                                                                            <!-- Staging: the clip tray that
                                                                                 owns the other end lands with
                                                                                 the Reels dashboard, so this
                                                                                 is a local toggle for now. -->
                                                                            <Button Grid.Column="3"
                                                                                    Classes="chip"
                                                                                    Command="{Binding StageCommand}"
                                                                                    FontSize="11" Padding="8 2"
                                                                                    MinWidth="30"
                                                                                    VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                                                                    ToolTip.Tip="Stage this clip for a reel">
                                                                                <Panel>
                                                                                    <TextBlock Text="+"
                                                                                        IsVisible="{Binding !IsStaged}" />
                                                                                    <TextBlock Text="✓"
                                                                                        IsVisible="{Binding IsStaged}"
                                                                                        Foreground="{DynamicResource StatPositive}" />
                                                                                </Panel>
                                                                            </Button>
                                                                            <Button Grid.Column="4" Classes="ghost"
                                                                                    IsVisible="{Binding VerifyPresent}"
                                                                                    IsEnabled="{Binding CanVerify}"
                                                                                    Command="{Binding VerifyCommand}"
                                                                                    FontSize="11" Padding="8 2"
                                                                                    VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                                                                    ToolTip.Tip="Play this moment live in CS2 (spectating the player)">
                                                                                <Panel>
                                                                                    <TextBlock Text="Verify live"
                                                                                        IsVisible="{Binding !IsVerifying}" />
                                                                                    <StackPanel
                                                                                        Orientation="Horizontal"
                                                                                        Spacing="5"
                                                                                        IsVisible="{Binding IsVerifying}">
                                                                                        <Ellipse Width="8" Height="8"
                                                                                            Classes="dot stateGood pulsing"
                                                                                            VerticalAlignment="Center" />
                                                                                        <TextBlock Text="Verifying…" />
                                                                                    </StackPanel>
                                                                                </Panel>
                                                                            </Button>
                                                                        </Grid>
                                                                    </Border>
                                                                </DataTemplate>
                                                            </ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
                                                        </ItemsControl>
                                                    </Expander>
                                                </DataTemplate>
                                            </ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
                                        </ItemsControl>
                                    </ScrollViewer>
                                </DockPanel>
                            </Border>
                        </StackPanel>

                        <!--
                            ENRICHMENTS — the extension slot. An enrichment is a ViewModelBase + a matching
                            View appended to EnrichmentSections; the app ViewLocator resolves it, so adding
                            one costs ZERO edits to this file. The slot is in the tree from frame one and
                            renders zero height when empty, and enrichments register at COMPOSITION rather
                            than streaming in mid-load — an enrichment that appeared while a load was running
                            would reintroduce exactly the layout jump this page exists to prevent.
                            (Collection lands with the Reels dashboard; the slot is reserved here.)
                        -->
                    </StackPanel>
                </Grid>

            </StackPanel>
        </ScrollViewer>

    </Panel>
</UserControl>